# 🌤️ Weather App

A simple and interactive weather application built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

The app allows users to search for any city and display its current temperature, wind speed, and weather conditions.

## 📸 Screenshot

![Weather App Screenshot](screenshot.png)

## 🚀 Live Demo

[View Live Demo](https://wijdane-09.github.io/My-Own-Projects/weather-app/)

## ✨ Features

- 🔎 Search for any city
- 🌡️ Display current temperature
- 💨 Display wind speed
- ☁️ Display current weather conditions
- 📅 Display the current date
- 💾 Save the last searched city using LocalStorage
- 📱 Responsive design

## 🛠️ Technologies

- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript
- Fetch API
- Async / Await
- JSON
- LocalStorage

## 🔄 How It Works

1. The user enters a city name.
2. The app sends the city name to the Geocoding API.
3. The API returns the city's latitude and longitude.
4. The app uses these coordinates with the Weather API.
5. The weather data is returned as JSON.
6. The app displays the city, temperature, wind speed, and weather conditions.
7. The searched city is saved in LocalStorage.

## 🌐 APIs

This project uses the Open-Meteo APIs:

- Geocoding API — to find the latitude and longitude of the city.
- Weather API — to retrieve the current weather data.

